# Dev Notes 49 — Runtime Backend Adapter Execution Interface v1

**Date:** 2026-06-18  
**Branch:** `runtime-backend-adapter-execution-interface-v1`  
**Status:** Merged to `main` and main-inspected for the declared contract/interface-only scope; assistant sandbox syntax checks, targeted backend-adapter execution-interface smoke, existing contract-chain smokes, fixture helper check, worker import-cycle check, public-entrypoint guard, artifact guard, package extraction/recheck, Michael-run local Windows/MINGW64 candidate checks, direct GitHub branch inspection, and direct GitHub `main` inspection passed. No real-runtime test is required for the declared contract/interface-only scope because this branch does not touch runtime/worker/lifecycle/native execution surfaces.

---

## 1. Purpose

This branch adds a narrow backend adapter invocation descriptor seam after the existing capability execution / executor skeleton descriptor chain.

The descriptor chain becomes:

```text
actionEnvelope
  -> capability bus action
  -> router route plan
  -> service plan
  -> backend adapter plan
  -> capability execution plan
  -> executor skeleton handoff descriptor
  -> backend adapter invocation descriptor
```

The new backend adapter invocation descriptor is minimal and backend-facing. It is derived from a validated capability execution plan or a validated executor skeleton handoff descriptor.

This branch does not execute adapters.

It does not call services, call backend adapters, call `workerBridge`, import `llama_worker`, enqueue runtime requests, stream tokens, load models, or touch worker/lifecycle behavior.

---

## 2. Design decision

Selected input design:

```text
Use a smaller backend adapter invocation descriptor derived from the validated upstream execution/skeleton chain.
```

The backend adapter execution interface does not consume raw action envelopes, raw backend adapter definitions, or raw backend adapter plans directly.

Raw backend adapter plans remain upstream source material for capability execution validation, not direct invocation inputs.

This preserves the intended layering:

```text
Capability Bus / Router / Service / Executor validate and decide what should happen
Backend Adapter Invocation Descriptor carries only the backend-facing invocation contract
Backend Adapter may execute later in a separate behavior-wiring branch
```

