## 4. Contract behavior

The new backend adapter invocation descriptor helpers:

```js
validateBackendAdapterInvocationDescriptor(value)
normalizeBackendAdapterInvocationDescriptor(value)
assertBackendAdapterInvocationDescriptor(value)
```

Behavior:

```text
accepts a current capability execution plan
accepts a current executor skeleton handoff descriptor
accepts an already normalized backend adapter invocation descriptor
normalizes accepted sources to a minimal backend adapter invocation descriptor
copies normalized invocation metadata
requires contract-only / non-executable boundary metadata
rejects raw backend adapter plans as direct invocation inputs
rejects unknown top-level, invocation, and boundary fields
rejects forbidden executable/raw backend/model-path/runtime/worker keys
returns copy-isolated normalized descriptors
```

Copied invocation metadata:

```text
actionId
runId
capability
serviceId
adapterId
backendKind
routeId
modelBundleId
hardwareProfileId
stream
timeoutMs
resultContract
eventContract
```

---

## 5. Architecture boundaries preserved

This branch does not:

```text
change runtime.mjs public APIs
add executeAction() behavior
call capability services
invoke backend adapters
call workerBridge
import llama_worker
load models
enqueue runtime requests
stream tokens
change scheduler/request/stream behavior
change cancellation or timeout behavior
change lifecycle/init/reset/shutdown behavior
expand configOverride
add request-time raw model paths or projector paths
accept raw backend payloads, commands, handlers, execute/invoke functions, or backend options
implement memory/storage behavior
implement Cognitive Graph Runtime behavior
implement multimodal/vision execution
```

The backend adapter invocation descriptor remains a contract-only target for a later behavior-wiring branch.

